  "text": {
    "markdown": "## Support chat: quick satisfaction survey\n\nFive short questions, about a minute. Send this to the customer right after the chat ends.\n\n---\n\n**Thanks for chatting with us. How did we do?**\n\n**1. Overall, how satisfied are you with the support you just received?**\n1 – Very dissatisfied · 2 – Dissatisfied · 3 – Neutral · 4 – Satisfied · 5 – Very satisfied\n\n**2. Did we resolve your issue?**\nYes · Partly · No\n\n**3. How easy was it to get the help you needed?**\n1 – Very difficult · 2 – Difficult · 3 – Neither · 4 – Easy · 5 – Very easy\n\n**4. How likely are you to recommend us to a friend or colleague?**\n0 (not at all likely) to 10 (extremely likely)\n\n**5. Anything else you would like to tell us?** *(optional)*\nIf you scored us 1 or 2 on the first question: what went wrong?\nOtherwise: what is one thing we could have done better?\n\n*May we contact you about your feedback?* Yes / No\n\n---\n\n### Why these questions\n\n| # | Measures | Metric |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Satisfaction with this interaction | **CSAT**: share of 4s and 5s |\n| 2 | Whether the problem is actually fixed | **Resolution rate** |\n| 3 | How much effort it took | **CES** (customer effort score) |\n| 4 | Loyalty to the company overall | **NPS**: % scoring 9–10 minus % scoring 0–6 |\n| 5 | The reason behind the scores | Free text for follow-up |\n\n### Tips for sending it\n\n- **Send it immediately**, while the chat is still fresh. People are far more likely to answer in the moment than later.\n- **Keep question 1 first and answerable in one tap.** Many people stop there, and that single answer is still useful.\n- **Follow up on low scores.** A 1 or 2, or a \"No\" on question 2, should open a ticket for a human to review.\n- **Do not add more questions.** Each extra one costs completions.\n",
    "validation": {
      "valid": true,
      "checks": [
        "is non-empty Markdown",
        "contains no raw HTML outside code (react-markdown would print it literally)"
      ],
      "errors": [],
      "warnings": []
    }
  },
